<title>USA: Matritech starts trials of colorectal test.</title>
<headline>Matritech starts trials of colorectal test.</headline>
<dateline>NEWTON, Mass. 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matritech Inc said Wednesday it has begun clinical trials to obtain U.S. Food and Drug Administration approval for selling its colorectal cancer test in the United States.</p>
<p>Matritech said this is the second Nuclear Matrix Protein-based immunoassay it has developed. A pilot study showed the test to be more than twice as sensitive as the FDA-approved carcinoembryonic antigen assay in identifying colorectal cancer, the company said.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to start selling the test outside the U.S. this year.</p>
<p>Separately, the company said Yamanouchi Pharmaceuticals Co Ltd won't be Matritech's distribution partner for the colorectal test in Japan and it is talking to other possible distributors.</p>
</text>
